'''''Sideritis romana''''', the '''simplebeak ironwort''', is a species of shrub in the family [[Lamiaceae]]. They have a self-supporting growth form and simple, broad leaves. Flowers are visited by [[European wool carder bee]], [[Rhodanthidium septemdentatum]], Amegilla, and [[Osmia andrenoides]]. Individuals can grow to 0.15 m.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Sideritis romana L. - Encyclopedia of Life|url=https://eol.org/pages/579350|access-date=2022-02-04|website=eol.org}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Mifsud |first=Stephen |date=2002-08-23 |title=Sideritis romana (Common Siderits) : MaltaWildPlants.com - the online Flora of the Maltese Islands. |url=https://www.maltawildplants.com/LABT/Sideritis_romana.php |access-date=2022-03-07 |website=www.maltawildplants.com |language=en-us}}</ref>

